# Data tables

Use [Material data tables](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/data-tables/) for field references and other tabular data. Markdown tables are supported. Do not add tablesort, a CSV or Excel import plugin, or extra CSS.

A field reference uses these columns, in this order: Field, Type, Default, Description. Put the field name in backticks. Write `required` in Default when the field must be set, and `none` when it is optional and has no default.

```markdown
| Field | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `gap` | number | `5` | Space between columns, in mm. |
```

- Cells may contain inline code, links, and other inline Markdown.
- Leave every column left-aligned. The divider is `| --- |`.
- Center a column with `:---:` and right-align it with `---:` only when the values are numbers that should line up. Field tables stay left-aligned.
- One header row. Do not merge cells or add a second header.
- Keep each row on one line.
